{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c477","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07bd4-2401-7280-a034-9d657f7825ef"},"sequence":150,"recorded_at":1780531400000295,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c2c31914-ab73-4f56-a747-9109399dc0be","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"c2c31914-ab73-4f56-a747-9109399dc0be","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c2c31914-ab73-4f56-a747-9109399dc0be"},"call_id":"call_01a07bd46bc47710b7d0828d16229688","text":"Read text file `/tmp/verdict-rev1.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2z3se0 — reviewer verdict, CR-TASK-260830-2z3se0-1 revision 1\n2|\n3|- Verdict: **changes requested** → `to-dev`\n4|- repeat-of: `none` (first revision of this element)\n5|- Reviewed tree: `560edb5038899378e1280358248f2513054ea9df` (base `1cb6b93585749df4ef4755ce93e486bcde9e3a6b`), `repository_delta=present`, 29 paths.\n6|- Working-tree OID verified equal to the candidate tree before and after every mutation batch; the mutation harness restored `internal/sessadapter`, `internal/traceability`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` from a pre-run copy after each run and the OID is unchanged.\n7|\n8|## Baseline facts reproduced by this run\n9|\n10|| Check | Result |\n11|| --- | --- |\n12|| `go build ./...` | exit 0 |\n13|| `go vet ./internal/sessadapter/` | exit 0 |\n14|| `go test ./... -count=1` | 17/17 packages ok |\n15|| `go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -cover` | 81.1% of statements |\n16|| `go test ./internal/sessadapter/ -v` | 848 tests, 848 PASS |\n17|| refusal-arm inventory | 323 derived arms across 9 production files, 323/323 witnessed |\n18|| vocabulary census | 55 tables registered across 9 files |\n19|| member-set census | 20 closed bodies derived |\n20|| switch census | 4 classified switches |\n21|| operation table | 14 operations derived |\n22|| lone-surrogate sweep | 6144 vectors refused |\n23|| tracecheck | `acceptance_cases=88`, coverage line unchanged |\n24|\n25|## Traversal method and ratio\n26|\n27|Gates were discovered by traversing production source (`grep` over comparison\n28|sites, membership functions, member loops, and the eight-fact equality chains),\n29|not by following the test files. Each gate was attacked with a mutant that keeps\n30|the gate present and weakens it to admit one member of the class it must reject;\n31|delete-only mutants were used only where the reject class has a single member.\n32|Compile failures were re-anchored and re-measured, never counted as kills.\n33|\n34|**87 mutants applied and measured across 45 gate sites: 63 killed, 24 survived\n35|(72%).** One mutant (`CheckFreshSink` exempting `MaxObjects == 0`) is excluded as\n36|equivalent: `DecodeObjectAuthority` already refuses that combination, so no\n37|decoded authority can reach it.\n38|\n39|**Stated bound of this method:** it measures the gates reachable from this\n40|package's exported API. It says nothing about how a future caller sequences\n41|`Discover` → `CheckProbe` → `CheckTupleAdmission` → `CheckCallBinding`, because\n42|no in-repo caller exists yet — nothing outside `internal/sessadapter` imports the\n43|package. It also does not attack `internal/canonicaljson`, `internal/scalar`, or\n44|`internal/axerror`, which several gates delegate to.\n45|\n46|## Findings\n47|\n48|### F1 (blocking, G-A) — the closed-vocabulary census cannot see non-table vocabularies, and four production vocabularies already live in the blind spot\n49|\n50|`isVocabularyShape` (census_test.go:238) matches only an `*ast.CompositeLit`\n51|whose `Type` is `*ast.MapType` or `*ast.ArrayType`. Everything else is invisible.\n52|The file's own claim — \"The census finds the membership surface by parsing\n53|production source and fails closed on anything with no registered derivation, so\n54|the surface cannot grow something unwitnessed\" — does not hold.\n55|\n56|Shape probes (a two-member vocabulary consulted from production, three ways):\n57|\n58|| Probe | Shape | Census |\n59|| --- | --- | --- |\n60|| C1 | `var t = []string{...}` + membership loop | **KILLED** (`TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered`) |\n61|| C2 | `type s []string; var t = s{...}` + same loop | **SURVIVED** |\n62|| C3 | `if v == \"a\" \\|\\| v == \"b\"` | **SURVIVED** |\n63|\n64|C3's shape is already occupied. Four closed unions are checked inline and appear\n65|in neither `vocabularyRegistrations` nor `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec`:\n66|\n67|| Site | Union | Spec | Widening mutant |\n68|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n69|| `context.go:410` | `mode ∈ {read, fresh_sink}` | `<code>mode:read\\|fresh_sink</code>` (same ObjectAuthority sentence the census already parses for `purpose`) | `+reuse_sink` **SURVIVED** |\n70|| `tuple.go:1062` | entry `status ∈ {accepted, revoked}` | §13.14 entry sentence | `+expired` **SURVIVED** |\n71|| `tuple.go:526,622` | `result = pass` (fixture and resume-smoke) | `<code>result=pass</code>` | `+waived` **SURVIVED** |\n72|| `probe.go:592` | `direction ∈ {source_read, target_write}` | doctor row | `+hybrid` **SURVIVED** |\n73|| `probe.go:605` | `registry_entry_status ∈ {accepted, revoked, absent}` | doctor row, same `member:a\\|b\\|c` form as `fidelity_profile` and validate `mode`, both of which the census does pin via `rowInlineUnion` | `+pending` **KILLED**, but only because the witness happens to feed the literal `\"pending\"` — the union itself is unpinned |\n74|\n75|Control: widening a *table* vocabulary (`capabilityStatuses` + `\"deprecated\"`) is\n76|**KILLED** by `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec`. So the spec pin works; it just\n77|does not reach these five.\n78|\n79|The `mode` survivor is not only a census gap. A widened `mode` produces an\n80|`ObjectAuthority` that passes `DecodeObjectAuthority`, then silently skips\n81|`CheckFreshSink` (`context.go:526` returns nil for any mode ≠ `fresh_sink`) *and*\n82|the `mode == \"fresh_sink\" && (maxObjects == 0 || maxTotalBytes == 0)` coherence\n83|rule at `context.go:433`. A third mode name disables both halves of the fresh-sink\n84|authority with a green suite.\n85|\n86|**Failure scenario:** a later leaf adds `mode:read|fresh_sink|reuse_sink` (or any\n87|inline union) to production. Every test stays green, the census reports 55/55\n88|registered, `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec` reports nothing, and an authority\n89|mode the spec never defined bypasses the sink-emptiness and limits gates.\n90|\n91|### F2 (blocking, G-A) — the refusal-arm inventory's stated alias closure is false for `var x = ctor`\n92|\n93|inventory_test.go documents: \"Constructor references outside direct-call position\n94|(aliases, variables holding a constructor) fail the derivation outright: an\n95|aliased constructor hides every arm it builds.\" `collectFileArms` skips any\n96|constructor `*ast.Ident` whose parent is an `*ast.ValueSpec` — which is true of\n97|the *definition's* Name **and** of an alias's Value.\n98|\n99|| Probe | Form | Result |\n100|| --- | --- | --- |\n101|| inv01 (control) | new arm through a direct `failInvalid(...)` call | **KILLED** — `TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed` |\n102|| inv02 | `var plantedFail = failInvalid` at package level, arm built through it | **SURVIVED** |\n103|| inv03 | `var localFail = failInvalid` inside the function, arm built through it | **SURVIVED** |\n104|| inv04 | `localFail := failInvalid` | **KILLED** (parent is `AssignStmt`, so the alias gate does fire) |\n105|\n106|`var` is the form the package itself uses for these constructors, so it is the\n107|form a future producer would reach for. The 323/323 figure is therefore a count\n108|over the arms the derivation happens to see, and the closure claim behind it does\n109|not hold.\n110|\n111|**Failure scenario:** a producer writes `var failShape = failProtocol` and builds\n112|three refusal arms through it. The derivation returns 323 arms (still ≥ the\n113|census floor), all witnessed, both directions green — and three refusal arms ship\n114|with no witness and no assertion of their identity.\n115|\n116|### F3 (blocking, G-B) — the surrogate *pairing* bound is proven on neither edge\n117|\n118|`TestLoneSurrogateSweep` generates 6144 vectors and kills every mutant on the\n119|*first* surrogate: `first >= 0xD800` → `> 0xD800` KILLED, `<= 0xDBFF` → `<= 0xDBFE`\n120|KILLED, lone-low `<= 0xDFFF` → `<= 0xDFFE` KILLED. The *second* (low) surrogate in\n121|`hasLoneSurrogateEscape` has only three hand-written pair vectors\n122|(`😀`, `\\uD83DA`, and truncations), and both its edges survive:\n123|\n124|| Mutant (decode.go:107) | Admits | Result |\n125|| --- | --- | --- |\n126|| `second > 0xDFFF` -> `second > 0xDFFF+1` | `\"A\\uD800\\uE000B\"` -- a lone high surrogate followed by U+E000 | **SURVIVED** |\n127|| `second < 0xDC00` -> `second < 0xDBFF` | `\"A\\uD800\\uDBFFB\"` -- a high surrogate followed by another high surrogate | **SURVIVED** |\n128|\n129|Both admitted forms are lone surrogates that `encoding/json` then rewrites to\n130|U+FFFD — the exact silent byte-rewriting the gate exists to prevent, and the\n131|defect the pinned §1.6 rule is there to stop. This is the same shape the brief\n132|names from the prior Story (\"a hand-written vector corpus that cannot tell a\n133|correct bound from an off-by-one\"), moved one function inward.\n134|\n135|### F4 (blocking, G-B) — set-valued gates are proven on a sample, and one refusal arm hides N obligations\n136|\n137|Where a gate loops over a fixed member list, all members share one refusal-arm\n138|identity, so the arm inventory reads green at 323/323 while only the member the\n139|fixture happens to exercise is driven. Loop-truncation mutants:\n140|\n141|| Gate | Truncation | Result |\n142|| --- | --- | --- |\n143|| `CheckDoctorHealthy` required-capability loop (probe.go:671) | `required[:1]` | **SURVIVED** — `healthy=true` with `native_read_back`, `native_resume_plan`, `workspace_binding` all unusable is admitted; 1 of 4 proven |\n144|| `checkValidateNullability` archive branch (operations.go:607) | `targets[:3]` | **SURVIVED** — archive mode carrying a non-null `expected_target_native_session_id` is admitted |\n145|| `checkValidateNullability` staged/live branch (operations.go:618) | `targets[:3]` | **SURVIVED** — staged/live with a null `expected_target_native_session_id` is admitted |\n146|| `checkValidateResult` applicable-check loop (operations.go:1107) | drop `resume_surface_valid` | **SURVIVED** — `valid=true` with `resume_surface_valid=false` is admitted |\n147|| `checkValidateResult` nullable-bool loop (operations.go:1081) | drop `resume_surface_valid` | **SURVIVED** |\n148|| `CheckTargetWriteGates` adapter loop (probe.go:483) | drop `workspace_binding` | KILLED |\n149|| `CheckTargetWriteGates` provider loop (probe.go:492) | drop `native_resume` | KILLED |\n150|| `CheckDoctorHealthy` name-validation loop (probe.go:652) | `required[:1]` | KILLED |\n151|\n152|`CheckTargetWriteGates` shows the right discipline (`TestCheckTargetWriteGates`\n153|drives each member); `CheckDoctorHealthy`'s required set and the validate\n154|nullability rule do not.\n155|\n156|### F5 — the byte-for-byte context echo, this package's stated idempotency binding, is not proven against a same-length rebuilt context\n157|\n158|`CheckContextEcho` (context.go:217) narrowed to\n159|`!bytes.Equal(received.raw, sent.raw) && len(received.raw) != len(sent.raw)`\n160|**SURVIVED**. Any echoed context that differs in bytes but not in length — one\n161|flipped hex digit in `operation_id`, `request_digest`, or either digest — is\n162|admitted. `doc.go` names the byte-for-byte echo as one of the two properties that\n163|*are* this package's idempotency, and `session-adapter-idempotency` is one of the\n164|seven acceptance cases registered in `ownership.v0.5.0.json`.\n165|\n166|### F6 — the 8 MiB frame bound is unproven at its edge, in both directions\n167|\n168|`protocol.go` guards three frames with `len(frame) > MaxFrameBytes`. The fixture\n169|pads with `MaxFrameBytes` characters *inside* an envelope, so it lands ~200 bytes\n170|past the edge.\n171|\n172|| Mutant | Result |\n173|| --- | --- |\n174|| `> MaxFrameBytes` → `> MaxFrameBytes+1` (admits a frame of exactly 8 MiB + 1) | **SURVIVED** |\n175|| `> MaxFrameBytes` → `>= MaxFrameBytes` (refuses a frame of exactly 8 MiB, which §7.2 admits) | **SURVIVED** |\n176|\n177|Neither side of the stated limit is pinned.\n178|\n179|### F7 (non-blocking, name as a bound or fix) — equality gates over host-supplied facts are unproven for the zero-value fact\n180|\n181|`ProbeHostFacts`, `SuccessFacts`, and `TrustedCandidate` are plain structs with no\n182|constructor. `Discover` validates its candidate; `CheckProbe`, `CheckProbeRequest`,\n183|and `checkValidateResult` do not check that the host fact they compare against is\n184|populated. Baseline fails closed by accident of string comparison, but nothing\n185|pins it:\n186|\n187|- `probe.ProviderID != facts.ExpectedProviderID` → `&& facts.ExpectedProviderID != \"\"` **SURVIVED**\n188|- `probe.Environment.EnvironmentID != facts.Manifest.EnvironmentID` → `&& … != \"\"` **SURVIVED**\n189|- `expectedKind != candidate.Kind` → `&& expectedKind != \"\"` **SURVIVED**\n190|- `mode != facts.ValidateMode` → `&& facts.ValidateMode != \"\"` **SURVIVED**\n191|\n192|A caller that forgets one field currently gets a refusal; one test per gate would\n193|keep it that way.\n194|\n195|### F8 (bound, not a demand) — open-class member gates are witnessed with one hand-picked name\n196|\n197|`unknownMember` exempting one name (`&& name != \"debug\"`) and the duplicate-member\n198|gate exempting one name (`&& key != \"extensions\"`) both **SURVIVED**. The reject\n199|class is unbounded, so no single narrowing mutant is decisive here; recording it\n200|as a stated bound of the arm inventory is enough.\n201|\n202|## Evidence-quality finding\n203|\n204|The attached `verification-evidence.log` reports `killed-or-green=8 unexpected=0`\n205|from five mutants (M1 `capabilityStatuses` widened, M2 `findingSeverities`\n206|widened, M3 `requestMembers` widened, M4/M4b `validCapabilityStatus` return-true,\n207|M5 unregistered vocabulary table). None are delete-only — that part is right —\n208|but all five land on the *table*-shaped surface that is already spec-pinned, and\n209|the run reports no killed/measured ratio over a gate traversal. The DoD row\n210|\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant\" is checked against evidence\n211|covering 5 of ~45 gate sites. The independent traversal above found 24 survivors,\n212|six of which are behavioral.\n213|\n214|## What is correct and should not be re-litigated\n215|\n216|- **G-C traceability is sound.** The 81 → 88 re-pin is computed, not copied:\n217|  editing a single acceptance-case declaration reddens with an exact digest\n218|  mismatch (`ownership registry projection digest %s differs from reviewed %s`),\n219|  and renaming a production declaration is refused by\n220|  `TestVerifyRepositoryRejectsForgedOwnershipAndCapabilityClaims`. All seven new\n221|  rows name declarations that exist. The README §7.8 paragraph is true of the\n222|  tree: `section:7.8` is still bound to `catalog.ForRelease` with\n223|  `coverage: \"unevidenced\"`, the coverage line is byte-identical before and after,\n224|  and the README says so rather than claiming clause coverage the registry does\n225|  not carry.\n226|- **The operation-body derivation is the right shape.** Probe points come from the\n227|  pinned document and verdicts from production;\n228|  `TestOperationBodiesRefuseDerivedMutations` drops every derived member in turn.\n229|  Dropping a member from `requestBodyMembers` or `successBodyMembers` is killed\n230|  from three directions.\n231|- **Bounds are character-counted and two-sided.** `checkStringBounds` and\n232|  `checkUint53Bounds` die on `maximum+1` and on `minimum-1`, and\n233|  `TestDecodeManifestValueRules` carries both an ASCII and a multibyte 129-character\n234|  fixture — the byte-vs-character defect from the prior Story is closed.\n235|- **The eight-fact binding equality is complete.** Deleting each of the eight facts\n236|  in `CheckBindingEquality` is killed 8/8 by `TestBindingEqualityFlipsEveryFact`.\n237|- **Refusal arms assert their identity.** Every `valid*` membership function\n238|  neutralised by a token-preserving `return true` is killed 14/14, and the failing\n239|  witness names the arm (code + distinguishing detail), not merely \"something\n240|  refused\". The 0-of-29 defect from the prior Story is closed.\n241|- Registry order, sorted-unique strictness, capability count, tuple admission\n242|  (status, validity upper edge, `archive_only` exactly-one, missing smoke),\n243|  capability coherence, validate structural/semantic and error-finding rules,\n244|  resource-limit cross rules, UTF-8 and trailing-data gates: all killed.\n245|\n246|## Requested changes\n247|\n248|1. **F1** — pin `mode`, `registry_entry_status`, entry `status`, `direction`, and\n249|   `result=pass` against their pinned-document spans (all five are in the\n250|   `<code>member:a|b|c</code>` or `<code>member=value</code>` form the census\n251|   already parses elsewhere), and close the census shape gap so a vocabulary\n252|   declared through a named type or an inline comparison chain cannot be added\n253|   unregistered. Correct the census doc comment to match what the scanner sees.\n254|2. **F2** — treat a constructor identifier appearing as a `ValueSpec` *Value* as an\n255|   alias and fail the derivation, keeping the definition's *Name* exempt. Re-run\n256|   the inv02/inv03 probes as regression witnesses.\n257|3. **F3** — generate the surrogate *pair* corpus the way the lone corpus is\n258|   generated: for each high surrogate, sweep the second escape across the low\n259|   range and both adjacent code points, so `\\uD800\\uE000` and `\\uD800\\uDBFF`\n260|   refuse by construction.\n261|4. **F4** — drive every member of each set-valued gate, or split the arm so each\n262|   member carries its own detail. `CheckDoctorHealthy` (all four required\n263|   capabilities) and `checkValidateNullability` (all four targets, both branches)\n264|   are the load-bearing ones.\n265|5. **F5** — add a same-length, different-bytes context echo case.\n266|6. **F6** — pin the frame bound at exactly `MaxFrameBytes` (admitted) and\n267|   `MaxFrameBytes + 1` (refused).\n268|7. **F7** — either add the zero-value host-fact cases or record the bound\n269|   explicitly.\n270|8. **Evidence** — report the mutant battery as a killed/measured ratio over a\n271|   traversal of production gate sites, and name what the method cannot see.\n272|\n273|No stop-the-line boundary was found: every finding is ordinary rework inside this\n274|package's own scope, with no external platform, product, or ownership decision\n275|required.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
