{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c69b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07bd4-2401-7280-a034-9d657f7825ef"},"sequence":424,"recorded_at":1780531400000843,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c2c31914-ab73-4f56-a747-9109399dc0be","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"c2c31914-ab73-4f56-a747-9109399dc0be","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c2c31914-ab73-4f56-a747-9109399dc0be"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"0bde46b4-29d2-4043-823f-4b421d18d8a1"},"task_id":"0bde46b4-29d2-4043-823f-4b421d18d8a1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"0bde46b4-29d2-4043-823f-4b421d18d8a1","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-11-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"sessrepo\\\\|mutation\\\\|12 applied\\\\|12/12\\\\|battery\\\" README.md | head -n 30; echo ===; grep -n \\\"sessrepo\\\\|wbpf1v\\\" LOGBOOK.md | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Find README battery and logbook sections\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"86:idempotent and isolated from caller mutation. It deliberately adds no `ax`\\n300:holding stale bytes. The specification is silent about that mutation, so the\\n460:the passed authority with no host-side mutation cache.\\n475:`(operation, operation_id)` mutation key (keyed operations derived\\n476:per-row from the Section 7.5 table). A lost mutation retried with\\n716:| Conformance fixtures | Story suites on Ubuntu and macOS | Exact fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass per platform, with skip lines as the skip datum; crash/idempotency evidence comes from the Transactor battery in this matrix |\\n717:| Fuzz smoke | Targets derived per package from the compiled test binaries (`secconftest`, `canonicaljson`, `scalar`), each smoked briefly; the `secconftest` leg is diffed against the `cigate.FuzzTargets` derivation | Every derived target executed its engine, proven by its elapsed line rather than by exit status alone. At `-fuzztime=100x` the large-corpus targets (`secconftest/FuzzRedactCorpus`, all four `canonicaljson` targets) spend the budget on baseline coverage and never reach the mutation phase: green proves engine execution, not mutation |\\n1062:No behavioural claim here depends on a mutation sweep; the sweep is an audit of\\n1354:These sweeps are audited by a recorded mutation run over the production sources.\\n1374:members plus Session Record envelope/member mutations, chunk rules, malformed\\n1385:so crash recovery and mutation idempotency are not applicable to these entry\\n1614:[`internal/sessrepo`](internal/sessrepo) persists and validates Session Records\\n1654:go test ./internal/sessrepo -count=1\\n1655:go test ./internal/sessrepo -cover -count=1\\n1667:include an import alias and a var binding in both directions. The mutation\\n1668:battery (12 applied, 12 killed, 0 survivors; 6 narrowing, 4 arm-deletion, 1\\n2149:mutation that moves both. This path needs no process at all - `DecodeBound`\\n===\\n8:### wbpf1v: session repository + event chain landed; provhost attestation bound rewritten around the new truth\\n9:- SCOPE: TASK-260830-wbpf1v (first leaf of STORY-260830-3tq4ns, root of M1 chain). New `internal/sessrepo` (doc/sessrepo/chain/store + behavioral/crash/census tests), README section, `internal/provhost/identity.go` comment + `identity_test.go` gate rewrite. Work left uncommitted in the story worktree for the board CR.\\n10:- FINDING (gate did its job): `go test ./...` reddened on `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`, which pins \\\"no production file calls VerifyObjectIdentity\\\". Session-record/event persistence MUST attest (SPEC §5.1/§5.2 \\\"MUST recompute and MUST reject\\\"); routing through `CalculateObjectIdentity` would dodge the text scan while attesting anyway, so the bound was rewritten, not bypassed: `internal/sessrepo/` allowlisted (schema gate precedes every Verify call, so provider-identity records can never reach one), every other tree still red (proved by a temporary foreign call site, then removed), exception fails when stale. Reviewers read the provhost diff first.\\n12:- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260830-wbpf1v_outcome.md` on the board task (10/10 AC rows with call sites, gate table, census + 12/12 killed mutation battery with narrowing/arm-deletion/census-only/audit-only + NOT_APPLIED/COMPILE_FAIL rows, tree OID + exact changed paths recorded there). Battery harness at `/tmp/mutation_battery.sh` (throwaway, not committed).\\n13:- GATES: `go test ./...` exit 0 (24 ok), `-race` exit 0 (all 24 pkgs, 4 groups), `-cover` (sessrepo 86.3/provhost 86.0), `go vet` + `GOOS=windows` vet/build exit 0, gofmt clean, tracecheck exit 0, catalog current, cigate contract + claims selections exit 0, fuzz count 13 (smoke not run: no fuzzed package touched).\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3712,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 928,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}}
