{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c71f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07bd4-2401-7280-a034-9d657f7825ef"},"sequence":490,"recorded_at":1780531400000975,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"c2c31914-ab73-4f56-a747-9109399dc0be","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"c2c31914-ab73-4f56-a747-9109399dc0be","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"c2c31914-ab73-4f56-a747-9109399dc0be"},"call_id":"call_01a07bd4eb777fe3908ab0affd70c6bb","text":"Read text file `/tmp/wbpf1v-outcome.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-wbpf1v outcome: session repository and event chain\n2|\n3|## Result\n4|\n5|`internal/sessrepo` implements durable Session Records and append-only\n6|per-session event chains with source sequence continuity (AX v0.5.0\n7|§2.3 local steps, §5.1–5.2, §5.7/§14.4 stored facts). Handbook handoff:\n8|to-review. Candidate tree OID (detached-index `write-tree` over exactly\n9|the paths below): `93942f4c8f07a865c546516c1be50b82f9c4e4e6`.\n10|\n11|## Changed paths (exactly the CR content)\n12|\n13|- `README.md` (new `Session Repository and Append-Only Event Chain` section)\n14|- `LOGBOOK.md` (flight entry for the bound rewrite)\n15|- `internal/provhost/identity.go` (bound comment rewrite, no behavior change)\n16|- `internal/provhost/identity_test.go` (attestation-gate rewrite, see §Finding)\n17|- `internal/sessrepo/doc.go` (scope, authority split, stated bounds)\n18|- `internal/sessrepo/sessrepo.go` (Repository, Open, CreateSession, AppendEvent)\n19|- `internal/sessrepo/chain.go` (decode layers, checkAppend, load/verify, atomic writes)\n20|- `internal/sessrepo/store.go` (Get/List/Resolve reads)\n21|- `internal/sessrepo/sessrepo_test.go` (behavioral battery)\n22|- `internal/sessrepo/crash_test.go` (secconftest crash/idempotency evidence)\n23|- `internal/sessrepo/census_test.go` (invcore census, TestMain gate, plants)\n24|\n25|No untracked ungitignored scratch file is present (`git status` shows only\n26|the three modified files plus the new `internal/sessrepo/` deliverable).\n27|\n28|## AC coverage: 10 of 10 rows driven through production entries\n29|\n30|| # | AC row | Production call site | Named driving test(s) |\n31||---|---|---|---|\n32|| 1 | Persist Session Records | `(*Repository).CreateSession` | `TestCreateSessionPersistsSpecRecordFixture`, `TestSessionRecordReloadsByteIdenticallyAcrossProcessBoundary` |\n33|| 2 | Validate Session Records | `(*Repository).CreateSession` | `TestCreateSessionRefusesMalformedFrame`, `...ForeignSchema`, `...MissingSessionID`, `...DigestMismatch` |\n34|| 3 | Appends succeed in order | `(*Repository).AppendEvent` | `TestAppendEventChainInOrder` |\n35|| 4 | No rewrite/delete path | `CreateSession`/`AppendEvent` (no update/delete entry exists) | `TestCreateSessionRefusesDuplicateAndRewrite`, `TestAppendEventRefusesSequenceRepeat` |\n36|| 5 | Gap refused (named arm, at edge) | `checkAppend` via `AppendEvent` | `TestAppendEventRefusesSequenceGap` (skip, first-past-one edge, successor-past-one, SPEC stopped fixture) |\n37|| 6 | Repeat refused (named arm) | `checkAppend` via `AppendEvent` | `TestAppendEventRefusesSequenceRepeat` (two-events-at-one-sequence) |\n38|| 7 | Exact contract fixtures pass | `CreateSession`/`AppendEvent` | SPEC §5.1 direct record accepted with digest `d617…`, task_board record with digest `0acd…`, both chained and co-listed (`TestBothRecordKindsCoexist`); SPEC §5.2 stopped event verifies and is refused as gap, never as invalid |\n39|| 8 | Negative/refusal cases pass | all entries | 34-site census, every site boundary-driven (see §Census) |\n40|| 9 | Crash/idempotency evidence | `BeforeWrite`/`AfterCommit` hooks | 4 crash tests via owner `secconftest` points (see §Crash) |\n41|| 10 | No unsupported capability | API surface (`go doc`: only `Repository` entries; no command/doctor/result wiring) | stated bound with surface evidence; README claims only what exists and passes `cigate` claims gates |\n42|\n43|## Gates actually run (exit codes observed in this session)\n44|\n45|| Gate | Exit |\n46||---|---|\n47|| `go build ./...` | 0 |\n48|| `go vet ./...` | 0 |\n49|| `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` | 0 |\n50|| `GOOS=windows go build ./...` | 0 |\n51|| `gofmt -l internal/` | clean |\n52|| `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | 0 (contracts=60, acceptance=98) |\n53|| `go test ./... -count=1` | 0, all 24 packages ok |\n54|| `go test ./... -count=1 -cover` | 0 (sessrepo 86.3%, provhost 86.0%) |\n55|| `go test -race` over all 24 packages (4 sequential groups) | 0 |\n56|| catalog freshness (`go generate` + `git diff --exit-code`) | 0, current |\n57|| `cigate` contract-version gates (6 named) | 0 |\n58|| `cigate` README capability-claims gates (6 named) | 0 |\n59|| fuzz target count (`-list '^Fuzz'` = 13) | 0, no drift |\n60|| `cigate` fuzz-derivation gates (2 named) | 0 |\n61|\n62|Not run: full fuzz smoke (`-fuzztime=100x` over 13 targets). Rationale:\n63|this change adds no fuzz target and modifies no fuzzed package\n64|(`secconftest`, `canonicaljson`, `scalar` untouched); the smoke is a\n65|CI-lane activity on unchanged surface.\n66|\n67|## Census (production-derived denominator, invcore)\n68|\n69|- Derived `refuse(` sites: **34** (sessrepo.go 5, chain.go 23, store.go 6).\n70|- Exercised beneath a boundary entry: **34 of 34**; exercised-outside: 0.\n71|- Sentinel roster derived from `Err*` vars: 14 texts; observed codes match\n72|  exactly. Six unreachable-by-construction candidates were removed from\n73|  production rather than planted around (identity-field re-checks after a\n74|  schema gate, impossible post-stat install conflicts, TOCTOU re-read).\n75|- Alias audit (`refuse` + 8 watched owner delegations) clean; unrouted\n76|  `fmt.Errorf`-with-sentinel audit clean.\n77|- Control plants, all asserting fail-closed: DiffSets unregistered site,\n78|  orphan row, zero-site derivation; alias audit with import-alias\n79|  direct-call (clean), import-alias var binding (fails), local var binding\n80|  (fails), dot import (fails), shadowed name (fails); unparseable plant\n81|  (harness fails).\n82|\n83|## Mutation battery (production-derived denominator: 34 sites)\n84|\n85|12 applied, **12 killed**, 0 survivors. Audit-only and census-only kills\n86|are separate classes, never folded into behavioural kills.\n87|\n88|| Mutant | Class | What it narrows | Named killing test |\n89||---|---|---|---|\n90|| N1 `> want` → `> want+1` | narrowing | gap arm admits gap-of-1 | `TestAppendEventRefusesSequenceGap` |\n91|| N2 `< want` → `+1 < want` | narrowing | repeat arm admits exact repeat | `TestAppendEventRefusesSequenceRepeat` |\n92|| N3 `!= 1` → `< 1` | narrowing | first-link admits extra predecessors | `TestAppendEventRefusesFirstPredecessorMismatch` |\n93|| N4 contains-tail → non-empty | narrowing | predecessor arm admits wrong link | `TestAppendEventRefusesLaterPredecessorMismatch` |\n94|| N5 schema gate admits session-event | narrowing | record gate admits one foreign class member | `TestCreateSessionRefusesForeignSchema` |\n95|| N6 fold A–Z → A–T | narrowing | ambiguity gate admits U–Z collisions | `TestResolveRefusesCaseFoldCollision` |\n96|| D1 delete gap arm | arm-deletion | — | `TestAppendEventRefusesSequenceGap` |\n97|| D2 delete repeat arm | arm-deletion | — | `TestAppendEventRefusesSequenceRepeat` |\n98|| D3 delete divergent arm | arm-deletion | — | `TestAppendEventPreservesDivergentBranchWithoutApplying` |\n99|| D4 delete idempotent branch | arm-deletion | — | `TestAppendEventIdempotentRetry` |\n100|| C1 funnel → direct `fmt.Errorf` (token preserved, behavior identical) | census-only | — | full-package run FAILs on `refusals raised outside the refuse funnel: chain.go:187` while behavioral tests PASS |\n101|| A1 unreachable extra `refuse` site | audit-only | — | full-package run FAILs on `refusal site without an exercised negative path: chain.go:195` while behavioral tests PASS |\n102|| X1 absent pattern | NOT_APPLIED | harness control | — (file untouched, proven by checksum) |\n103|| X2 broken syntax | COMPILE_FAIL | harness control | — (distinct from killed/survived) |\n104|\n105|Token-preserving-behavior-change mutants (C1 keeps the `ErrPredecessorLink`\n106|token while bypassing the funnel) are executed through the full behavioral\n107|suite plus the gate, never through the static checker alone.\n108|\n109|## Crash evidence (owner `secconftest` points, owner outcomes)\n110|\n111|- `PointPrepareEnter` armed on create: `*Fault(safe_retry)`; session stays\n112|  unknown; identical retry succeeds.\n113|- `PointPrepareEnter` armed on append: `*Fault(safe_retry)`; chain length\n114|  unchanged; retry appends at position 0.\n115|- `PointCommitApply` armed on create: `*Fault(recoverable_parked_state)`;\n116|  record reads back (crashed commit counts as committed); retry names the\n117|  terminal state (`ErrSessionExists`).\n118|- `PointCommitApply` armed on append: `*Fault(recoverable_parked_state)`;\n119|  event reads back; identical retry returns the committed reference with no\n120|  second chain entry; committed bytes survive a later refusal.\n121|- Resume path: record-without-chain completes on retry, then refuses as\n122|  existing. Reload across a second `Open` handle is byte-identical and the\n123|  chain continues there.\n124|\n125|## Finding: provhost attestation bound rewritten, not bypassed\n126|\n127|`go test ./...` reddened on\n128|`TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`: the gate pins \"no\n129|production file calls `VerifyObjectIdentity`\", and this leaf must call it\n130|(closed-shape + digest attestation for §5.1–5.2 has no other production\n131|entry; routing through `CalculateObjectIdentity` would dodge the text scan\n132|while attesting anyway — a bypass, rejected). Per the gate's own\n133|instruction the bound is rewritten around the new truth:\n134|`internal/sessrepo/` is allowlisted because it decodes the schema member\n135|first, so a provider-identity record dies at the schema gate before any\n136|`Verify` call; every other tree still fails (proved by a temporary foreign\n137|call site that reddened the gate, then removed); the exception fails when\n138|stale (zero allowlisted sites). `identity.go`'s comment is updated to match.\n139|Reviewers should read this diff first.\n140|\n141|## Reuse (no owner duplicates)\n142|\n143|Validation via `canonicaljson.VerifyObjectIdentity`; frame/member rules via\n144|`environ.DecodeStrictObject`/`CheckUUIDv7`/`CheckUint53Bounds`;\n145|grammars via `scalar.ParseDigest`/`ParseUUIDv7`/`ParseUUIDv4`;\n146|crash vocabulary via `secconftest` points/outcomes/`Fault`;\n147|census machinery via `invcore`. No new decoder, bound check, path policy,\n148|AST walker, or journal: atomicity is temp-file + fsync + rename + dir-fsync,\n149|and session IDs (UUIDv7 grammar) need no traversal guard beyond the scalar\n150|owner.\n151|\n152|## Stated bounds for downstream leaves\n153|\n154|Single authoritative branch per session (same-epoch second lease is\n155|preserved, never applied; arbitration is the leases story). No `SessionState`\n156|derivation (reducer leaf `1r9wrr`). No peer names or interactive choice\n157|(name-resolution leaf `21gygk`). No list rendering (CLI leaf). Chain index is\n158|a verified cache; blobs are truth.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
